1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,598
You have now built a robot by hand twice.

2
00:00:03,598 --> 00:00:08,736
In this short lesson you load one that NVIDIA prepared: Nova Carter,

3
00:00:08,736 --> 00:00:12,438
with physics, drives and a complete sensor suite.

4
00:00:13,338 --> 00:00:14,621
Loading it is easy.

5
00:00:14,621 --> 00:00:16,985
Start a new stage with a flat grid.

6
00:00:16,985 --> 00:00:20,226
Choose Create, Robots, Nova Carter with sensors.

7
00:00:20,226 --> 00:00:29,343
If you like, also open Window, Browsers, Isaac Sim Assets and search for carter to find the finished version of the robot you imported.

8
00:00:29,343 --> 00:00:35,150
The first load can take a few minutes, because the assets stream from NVIDIA's server.

9
00:00:36,050 --> 00:00:37,523
Expand chassis link.

10
00:00:37,523 --> 00:00:42,826
Under sensors you find two 2 D lidars, an RPLidar at the front and back,

11
00:00:42,826 --> 00:00:50,779
a Hesai X T thirty two 3 D lidar on top, four Hawk stereo cameras with I M Us, and four Owl fisheye cameras.

12
00:00:50,779 --> 00:00:55,198
Two driven wheel joints and two passive casters complete it.

13
00:00:55,198 --> 00:01:01,311
Notice that every sensor sits under the chassis body, exactly the rule you learned.

14
00:01:02,211 --> 00:01:08,059
In the console you may see warnings that the fisheye polynomial projection is deprecated.

15
00:01:08,059 --> 00:01:09,242
They are harmless.

16
00:01:09,242 --> 00:01:12,660
In module four you will drive this robot from ROS 2.

